{%- comment -%}
  ow-fonts — Neue Haas Display @font-face declarations, and the tokens that
  make NHD the only family the theme renders in.

  Lives in a snippet rather than in ow-base.css because asset_url is Liquid and
  plain .css assets are not rendered through Liquid. Rendered from layout/theme
  .liquid and layout/password.liquid, directly after `render 'css-variables'`,
  so the faces are declared on every page — including ones that do not render
  the ow-header section — and so the :root block below lands *after* the
  vendor's and wins the cascade at equal specificity, without !important.

  Source: neue-haas-grotesk-display-pro.zip, converted TTF -> woff2 with
  fontTools (395K -> 102K across the four weights).

  The family is exposed to CSS as 'NHD' — that is the name the --f token in
  ow-base.css expects. Weights map to the design's scale:

      900 Black   700 Bold   600 Medium   400 Roman

  Note the 600 face comes from NeueHaasDisplayMediu.ttf — the filename is
  truncated in the vendor zip, but its internal name is NeueHaasDisplay-Mediu
  and it is the Medium weight.

  font-display:swap renders fallback text immediately and swaps when the face
  arrives, so a slow font never blocks first paint. Type metrics shift slightly
  on swap; that is the intended trade against invisible text.

  The :root block overrides the two family tokens snippets/css-variables.liquid
  fills from the theme editor's font_picker settings. Every vendor stylesheet
  reads those two, so overriding them is what retires the picker fonts theme
  wide. --font-navigation-family, --font-button-family and --font-price-family
  are aliases of body/heading in css-variables, so they follow for free.

  Headings are Medium (600), body is Roman (400). Anything asking for bold text
  by name still resolves to the 700 face; 900 Black stays available to
  ow-base.css for display type.
{%- endcomment -%}

<style>
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'NHD';
    src: url({{ 'ow-nhd-black.woff2' | asset_url }}) format('woff2');
    font-weight: 900;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'NHD';
    src: url({{ 'ow-nhd-bold.woff2' | asset_url }}) format('woff2');
    font-weight: 700;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'NHD';
    src: url({{ 'ow-nhd-medium.woff2' | asset_url }}) format('woff2');
    font-weight: 600;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'NHD';
    src: url({{ 'ow-nhd-roman.woff2' | asset_url }}) format('woff2');
    font-weight: 400;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  :root {
    --font-body-family: 'NHD', 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    --font-body-style: normal;
    --font-body-weight: 400;

    --font-heading-family: 'NHD', 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    --font-heading-style: normal;
    --font-heading-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
